---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro'
import SectionHero from '../../components/SectionHero.astro'
import DocsMeta from '../../components/DocsMeta.astro'
import Callout from '../../components/Callout.astro'
import { ThemedShot } from '../../components/ThemedShot'
import { withBase } from '../../lib/path'
---
<DocsLayout title="Calendar" description="Every month of your reading as a calendar: what you read each day, how long, what you finished, and a card for any day you pick.">
  <SectionHero section="features" />
  <h1>Calendar</h1>
  <p>
    The Calendar is the month view of your reading. Each day you read shows the books you had
    open as small chips, with the day's total in the corner, and clicking a day opens a card with
    what that day looked like. It is built from the same session data
    as <a href={withBase("/docs/stats")}>Reading stats</a>: web reader sessions, everything the
    TomeSync KOReader plugin reports, and imported KOReader history.
  </p>
  <DocsMeta />

  <div class="docs-shot">
    <ThemedShot client:load name="calendar" alt="The Calendar page: a month grid with a chip per book read each day, the month's total hours above it, and a day card on the right" />
  </div>

  <h2>The month</h2>
  <p>
    Open <strong>Calendar</strong> from the sidebar. Above the grid is one number, the time you read
    that month, with the number of reading days under it and a line for your streaks and the books
    you finished. The grid is a plain calendar: weeks run Monday to Sunday, weekends are shaded, and
    the days of the neighbouring months fill the first and last week. Click one of those to jump
    to that month.
  </p>
  <p>
    A day with reading shows up to two chips, one per book, with the series and volume number
    where there is one, and <em>+1 more</em> when there were more. A chip with a check is a book you
    finished that day. The day's total time sits next to the date. Today is the accent-coloured
    circle, and the picked day is lifted slightly.
  </p>
  <p>
    Use the chevrons next to the month name to move around, or the arrow keys: left and right step
    a day, with Shift they step a month, <code>t</code> jumps back to today, and <code>Esc</code>
    closes the day. A <strong>Today</strong> button appears whenever you are on another month.
  </p>

  <h2>The day card</h2>
  <p>
    Pick a day and the card on the right fills in: a one-line summary of the day, badges for
    anything notable (a book finished or started, your biggest day of the month, where the day sits
    in a streak, reading past midnight), then the day's time, pages, number of sittings and pace.
  </p>
  <div class="docs-shot">
    <ThemedShot client:load name="calendar-day" alt="A day card: a summary line, badges, the day's totals, each book read with chapters and progress, and a timeline of when you read" />
  </div>
  <p>
    <strong>What you read</strong> lists each book with the time spent, pages, pace, the chapters
    you covered, and the progress you made that day on its bar. Under it, how that day's pace
    compares with your usual for that book. <strong>When</strong> is a timeline of the day's
    sittings from 4 am to 4 am, so a session that ran past midnight stays with the evening it
    belongs to.
  </p>
  <p>
    Books you had open for under a minute are not listed, though their time still counts toward
    the day's total. A book counts as finished on the day you marked it read, or the day its
    position first reached the end.
  </p>

  <Callout variant="info" title="On a phone">
    The grid is compact: the number of each day with a bar under it for how long you read. Tap a
    day and the card slides up as a sheet.
  </Callout>
  <figure style="margin: 1.5rem auto; max-width: 360px;">
    <ThemedShot client:load name="mobile-calendar-day" alt="The Calendar on a phone with a day's sheet open" />
  </figure>
</DocsLayout>
